WEBVTT

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.620
Both today and tomorrow, I've got time to kick back.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.620
kyou mo ashita mo HIMAKKUSU

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.830
My family of four and I are going to stay the night.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.830
gokazoku yonin de goippaku

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.670
Put on an Egyptian front and become a sphinx,

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.670
EGIPUTO kidori de SUFINKUSU

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.460
and for an American feeling, Texas!

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.460
AMERICA kibun de TEXAS

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.470
When you're sitting pretty, with enough and to spare,

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.470
yoyuu SHAKUSHAKUPPE itsumo

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.680
and yet you always shilly-shally,

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.680
funya funya de iruto

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.970
and your bitter face and bitter feelings both teeter-totter,

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.970
nigamushi hara no mushi nahe nahe to

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.390
it's time to get out of there!

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.390
tettai shichau yo

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.690
I am feeling Ultra Relax,

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.690
watashi ha URUTORA RIRAKKUSU

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.900
a wonderful, invincible Relax.

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.900
SUTEKI ni muteki na RIRAKKUSU

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.860
A one-step-above kind of Deluxe.

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.860
hito aji chigau ze DERAKKUSU

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:54.070
I may be a little jumbled,

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:54.070
toccharakatte mo

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:55.820
but when I'm called on, ba-ba-ba-ba-bang!

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:55.820
yobarerya PAPAPAPAAAN!

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.910
I always feel Relax,

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.910
watashi ha itsudemo RIRAKKUSU

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.910
a humble, simple, sort of Deluxe.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.910
WABISABI kikasete DERAKKUSU

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.830
Bright! Clear! Alert-headed, peep-peep!

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.830
BIKKARI! KIKKARI! saeteru ATAMA PII! PII!

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.960
Keep your eyes on me, okay?!

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.960
watashi no KOTO dake mitete ne!

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:36.700
My name is Kurata Sana, first year
Junior High School student.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:40.160
My manager and driver Rei-kun.

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:43.790
Mama, who's an award-winning
novelist, and Maro-chan her squirrel.

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:47.210
My buddy whom I met in
the bathroom Fuka.

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:49.920
The strange white bat, Babbit!

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:52.170
How old are you?

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:55.210
Naozumi-kun, who was with me in
New York honing our acting skills.

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:57.180
He's now my important partner.

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:00.850
Hayama Akito, my friend who's been
with me through thick and thin.

00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:03.140
He's now dating Fuka.

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:05.600
You are...

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:09.940
Let's...

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:13.230
break up.

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:19.240
Fight For It Or Break Up?
What Should We Do?

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:23.490
F-Fuka.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:30.790
Are you still mad about what
happened? That's not healthy for you.

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:32.250
I'm serious.

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:38.840
Anyway,
you need to get well quickly.

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:42.350
Akito.

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:44.760
I'll come again.

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:47.810
Akito!

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:54.980
I forgot my slippers.

00:02:55.570 --> 00:02:57.740
I brought a bag for my slippers.

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:00.860
Akito.

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:12.920
It's outrageous that an actor
can't say the lines in a script.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:14.460
That doesn't make any sense.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:15.880
Of course
we'd ask her to step down.

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:20.470
This drama is the brainchild of Mizoguchi-sensei and contains the emotions within our society.

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:23.930
It's not just
any regular school play...

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:27.390
Sensei's intentions are in every
sentence.

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:31.270
We can't create the desired conflict without using the word 'demon' in that scene.

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:34.270
There's no way to film this drama
without strong lines.

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:35.770
Isn't that so, Sensei?

00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:37.070
Correct.

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:40.360
Those words are very important...

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:43.490
...and cannot be replaced.

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:46.240
And that brat...

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:50.200
...that kid dared...

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:57.420
...dishonor me!

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:59.590
What and what?
Stop crying already.

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:03.470
Ah... a worm! A white worm!
I hate worms!

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:06.930
Sana-chan's never done this
sort of thing before.

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:10.930
She has let that little success on
Broadway go to her head.

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:16.560
I will never use that willful girl
who came back from N.Y. in any of my opus.

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:20.820
In fact, the entertainment world
in Japan will not use her anymore.

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:23.150
That's shocking news.

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:27.410
Has Sana-chan's willfulness gone
too far?

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:32.000
The Sana-chan who's caused
adults concern ever since her debut...

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.660
...has stepped over the line.

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:35.500
This is wrong.

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:38.590
Everyone had great expectations
for her career.

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:42.510
She may not be able to stay in
Japan's entertainment circle.

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:43.970
What a pity.

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:47.550
Bastards!
What do you mean 'what a pity'?!

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:49.430
What right
do you have to say that?

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:52.640
Don't they do that every time?
You should be used to it by now.

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:54.980
But Sensei! Doesn't it make you mad?

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:57.150
What's the use of yelling
like that?!

00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:59.610
Who's going to figure out
what to do?!

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:03.780
Kurata residence.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:05.700
What the hell are you thinking,
Kurata Sana?!

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:07.660
You're going to be finished
if you go on like this!

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:09.370
You idiot!

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:12.250
That kind of phone call again?

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:13.790
It's the 12th one today.

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:16.960
Let's give it a rest.

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:21.210
Sensei, you didn't have to cut the line! You could have just unplugged it!

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:24.010
That producer...

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:25.260
This one, this one.

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:27.260
...is pretty influential.

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:30.850
Sana-chan's acting career
may be over.

00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:35.350
Why can't Sana-chan say that word?

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:37.480
Even you don't know this?

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:39.770
Huh? Sensei, you know why?

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:43.320
The boy in the drama...

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:46.780
...is exactly like Hayama-kun was.

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:48.240
Hayama-kun?

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:54.580
Hayama-kun, who was insecure
because he grew up being called a demon.

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:58.250
At the time, Sana-chan put all
her effort...

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:00.500
Yes, she really did.

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:03.670
That's why we have Hayama-kun
the way he is now.

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:07.380
I heard Hayama-kun being called
a demon.

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:10.260
He even though he really was
a demon.

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:14.850
What an idiot. That's why he's such a gloomy character. It's too funny.

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:18.230
I'm going to make him laugh.

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:20.560
So he will say he's so happy
to be alive,

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:22.520
and laugh out loud.

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:30.030
I see, Sana-chan was afraid of
hurting Hayama-kun.

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:32.530
So that's it.

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:34.870
Ah, Sana-chan,
are you going out?

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:36.250
Yup, I have work to do!

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:37.460
Let's go, Rei-kun!

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:40.080
Oh, I forgot...

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:43.750
Isn't there a magazine interview?
The Dabara Weekly.

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:47.300
Ah, right, that's true.

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:49.340
But, it's okay if we turn it down.

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:50.800
Why?

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:57.220
At a time like this, it's probably
better not to accept an interview.

00:06:57.390 --> 00:06:59.310
What are you saying?

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:03.270
This is the time when we should
give interviews, don't you think, Rei-kun?

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:05.820
For you, for Naozumi-kun...

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:10.150
and for the people who work hard
on the set. I've made quite a lot of problems.

00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:13.030
But I feel that I'm not wrong.

00:07:13.030 --> 00:07:15.530
So I should lift my chin up.

00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:16.740
Let's go to work!

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:17.870
Sana-chan...

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:20.460
Let's go!

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:23.040
We're off, Sensei.

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:24.630
Off you go.

00:07:24.630 --> 00:07:25.840
Take care, Sagami.

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:27.210
White dolphin!

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:29.220
You don't have to keep me company.

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:31.090
Don't you have to prepare dinner?

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:33.470
But you can't see so I should
take care of you.

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:35.640
Alright, the apple's peeled.

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:37.430
I've put it next to the radio.

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:39.390
Okay, thanks.

00:07:39.390 --> 00:07:42.770
The nurse is here so I'll be okay.

00:07:44.110 --> 00:07:45.980
But your dad will be home
late today.

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:49.070
I don't have to rush home, so I'll
keep you company for dinner.

00:07:49.070 --> 00:07:50.570
Oh, alright...

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:55.240
Oh, did you put the covers out to
hang in the sun today?

00:07:56.660 --> 00:07:59.790
You haven't taken them in, have
you? What time is it now?

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:02.830
It's past 3! I'd better go home
and take them in.

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:05.840
Well, I guess I should go then,
I'm sorry!

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:06.840
It's okay.

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:08.550
I'll be here tomorrow morning.

00:08:09.260 --> 00:08:12.050
Ah my coat, my coat. And my purse!

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:14.720
Are you planning something?

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:18.930
She's gotten out of bed.

00:08:19.390 --> 00:08:21.430
She's going to the window.

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:25.980
The window's ready.

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:39.990
Now I won't look funny.

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:44.330
It's pretty tiring not being
able to see.

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:49.800
I should change.

00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:51.800
Alright.

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:55.090
What am I doing?

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:59.100
Am I waiting for Akito?

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:00.890
It's pretty obvious.

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:02.430
Here I am.

00:09:02.430 --> 00:09:05.440
What are you doing, you dork?!

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:06.690
Dork?

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:09.610
How can you just come into
a girl's room? Idiot.

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:10.440
Idiot?

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:12.070
You should at least warn me.

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:14.740
Didn't I just say I'm here?

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:16.490
I'm not saying...

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:18.910
Be careful! Ouch...

00:09:19.830 --> 00:09:21.660
Did you hurt yourself?

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:24.160
No, I'm okay.

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:31.420
What? Did you just laugh?

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:32.800
Nope.

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:34.010
This, this.

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:36.550
You're in pretty good spirits today.

00:09:36.970 --> 00:09:38.390
Grab hold.

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:43.180
I was worried about you.

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:47.390
But I guess I worried for nothing.

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:50.560
What's that supposed to mean?

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:52.900
Really, Akito...

00:09:56.700 --> 00:10:00.830
About what I said yesterday...

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:03.870
Can I have something to drink?

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:06.290
I ran all the way over here and
I'm thirsty.

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:09.000
There's hot tea in the thermos.

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:10.540
This is better.

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:11.590
Running here?

00:10:11.590 --> 00:10:13.090
Were you doing karate training?

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:16.170
Oh, you said you were going to have
a test soon.

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:17.630
Yeah.

00:10:18.220 --> 00:10:21.100
Will you be able to pass? Well,
will you be able to pass?

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:22.600
I guess.

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:25.430
Fuka-chan still doesn't know
Hayama's been suspended...

00:10:25.430 --> 00:10:29.100
...and can't take the karate test.

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:31.610
- Metropolitan.
- What are you saying?

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:34.070
- White dolphin!
- What white dolphin?

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:35.530
Hey, Akito.

00:10:35.530 --> 00:10:37.030
Can I have some apples?

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:38.740
I'm eating them.

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:40.700
People sent me all kinds of
food. Would you like some?

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:43.830
There's cake under the table and
sweet potatoes.

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:45.330
I can't eat all of it by myself.

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:49.330
- Didn't I tell you to be careful?
- Sorry.

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:50.830
How come your hair's a mess?

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:54.380
Has it been like this since...?

00:10:54.380 --> 00:10:56.420
Why didn't you tell me sooner?

00:10:56.420 --> 00:10:58.920
You don't have to get all
worked up.

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:01.800
Do you want to have some cake and
potatoes with me?

00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:06.430
Okay, I'll have some too.

00:11:06.430 --> 00:11:08.850
Will you still be able to eat
dinner?

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:15.020
Oh, don't worry.
The food here's terrible.

00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:18.740
I think you'll have to deal
with it today.

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:20.700
Why?

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:24.070
I don't feel like explaining.

00:11:24.070 --> 00:11:28.410
OK, I'll go to our favorite place
and get you a double cheeseburger tomorrow.

00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:29.540
Huh?

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:32.630
Okay.

00:11:33.420 --> 00:11:35.090
Uh, about tomorrow...

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:38.010
Akito? Akito?

00:11:47.180 --> 00:11:51.020
Why don't you use a nicer bag for
your slippers?

00:11:55.610 --> 00:12:06.620
{parte b}

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:12.000
Sana-chan,
your hair's so beautiful.

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:13.330
You must take good care of it.

00:12:13.330 --> 00:12:15.080
Really? But I don't, really.

00:12:15.210 --> 00:12:16.670
Is that so?

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:18.550
Looks like
the situation's gotten big.

00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:20.300
So spare us a little mercy.

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:24.180
What are you saying? You don't
have to worry about this type of thing.

00:12:24.180 --> 00:12:25.340
So you say...

00:12:25.340 --> 00:12:27.220
We're on your side.

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:29.970
We know there must be some
misunderstanding.

00:12:29.970 --> 00:12:33.520
Then please don't bring this
subject up in the interview.

00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:35.400
Sure, sure.

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:37.690
We're not that kind of magazine,
so don't worry.

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:39.020
Thanks, I appreciate it.

00:12:39.020 --> 00:12:41.400
An intabyuu is an interview.

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:46.280
So you grew quite a lot in
Broadway?

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:48.240
Yes, and it feels pretty good.

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:50.370
It's also a whole new arena.

00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:53.620
Compared to it,
Japan must be boring now.

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:55.330
Not at all.

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:59.800
On a separate note, do you feel
that you're an actress?

00:13:01.010 --> 00:13:02.300
You could say that...

00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:06.590
And since you're the lead role,
you must feel pretty proud of yourself.

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:10.220
Proud... I'd rather say I feel
responsible.

00:13:10.220 --> 00:13:12.270
Is it easy for you to get into
character?

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:15.440
How to say,
I'm not too sure myself.

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:20.320
And you can't help wanting to put
up a good show, right?

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:23.440
I guess that may create problems
for other people.

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:25.900
Do you get stubborn?

00:13:25.900 --> 00:13:27.280
This...

00:13:27.280 --> 00:13:29.700
I'm sorry, time's about up.

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:31.200
Just a little more.

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:36.290
I feel as an actress being
a little headstrong is alright.

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:40.630
Willfulness can be said to be an actress' natural instinct, don't you think?

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:45.010
Just because you're a child they say you're conceited and look down on adults.

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:46.760
Isn't this strange?

00:13:46.760 --> 00:13:47.970
Uh this...

00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:49.930
So you do look down on adults?

00:13:49.930 --> 00:13:51.060
Not at all!

00:13:51.060 --> 00:13:56.100
Isn't it true that since you were
little everyone's fussed over you.

00:13:56.980 --> 00:13:58.690
Just a little...

00:13:59.730 --> 00:14:01.940
Time's up. That's it for today.

00:14:01.940 --> 00:14:06.860
Sana, you have to express yourself.
You can't avoid the question.

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:09.620
You have to be more firm...

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:12.950
and tell everyone there's nothing
wrong with being arrogant.

00:14:13.240 --> 00:14:14.200
Sana, you also...

00:14:14.200 --> 00:14:17.080
That's enough. Didn't we agree
not to talk about this?

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:18.920
Did you ask her not to defend herself?

00:14:18.920 --> 00:14:19.830
You must be joking.

00:14:19.830 --> 00:14:21.710
If this goes on, the
misunderstanding won't go away.

00:14:21.710 --> 00:14:24.250
Why don't you let Sana-chan just
say it herself?

00:14:24.250 --> 00:14:26.340
You don't know anything.
What basis do you have to say that?

00:14:26.340 --> 00:14:28.720
That's why I'm asking.

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:30.050
Enough.

00:14:30.430 --> 00:14:32.810
Enough. Let's go home.

00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:35.770
Sana-chan.

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:39.980
Do you think we went too far?

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:44.110
Doesn't matter.
Just write a good article.

00:14:44.110 --> 00:14:46.320
We got our interview.

00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:49.110
- The rest is up to you.
- Right.

00:14:49.110 --> 00:14:52.200
Our magazine has to watch our
bottom line.

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:54.700
So we have to look after our
readers' interests.

00:14:57.200 --> 00:14:59.960
I'm sorry, Sana-chan, I...

00:15:01.130 --> 00:15:03.380
It's okay, Rei-kun.

00:15:03.380 --> 00:15:06.130
I never thought that was going to
happen.

00:15:06.130 --> 00:15:09.340
I believed that magazine publisher
and never thought they...

00:15:13.300 --> 00:15:14.850
Sana-chan,

00:15:14.850 --> 00:15:18.350
maybe this is a bad time to ask
you this...

00:15:18.350 --> 00:15:21.810
The fact that you can't say demon...

00:15:21.810 --> 00:15:23.480
...is it because...

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:27.820
There are lines...
you just can't say.

00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:29.030
Ok.

00:15:30.900 --> 00:15:32.410
He couldn't ask it.

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:33.660
White dolphin!

00:15:33.660 --> 00:15:35.370
Thank you for coming.

00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:46.130
Resignation?

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:49.300
If you don't know what Kouban is,
go check the dictionary.

00:15:49.300 --> 00:15:50.170
White dolphin!

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:51.470
I can't believe it.

00:15:51.470 --> 00:15:53.510
You got rid of me to meet that boy.

00:15:53.510 --> 00:15:55.430
I didn't get rid of you.

00:15:55.430 --> 00:15:59.600
The nurse saw him leaving by
the window.

00:15:59.600 --> 00:16:01.940
You should know what he's done.

00:16:02.350 --> 00:16:04.060
It wasn't his fault.

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:06.440
What are you saying, Fuka?

00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:08.650
My getting hurt wasn't his fault.

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:10.320
You and dad have misunderstood.

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:11.240
You...

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:12.490
He's not a bad person.

00:16:12.490 --> 00:16:14.240
Why don't you believe me?

00:16:14.240 --> 00:16:16.330
Fuka, stop it, Fuka.

00:16:16.330 --> 00:16:17.870
No!

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:21.660
Akito's not bad.

00:16:22.250 --> 00:16:25.290
But... but...

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:28.590
I also feel it's probably better
that I don't see him anymore.

00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:31.970
I'll tell him today when he comes.

00:16:31.970 --> 00:16:34.090
I'll explain it to him.

00:16:34.090 --> 00:16:35.890
So go home, mom.

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:38.760
Let me deal with this, please.

00:16:38.760 --> 00:16:40.520
Fuka.

00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:44.020
Alright, since you've decided.

00:16:46.730 --> 00:16:49.690
I won't see him again.

00:16:50.280 --> 00:16:52.030
Though I still want to...

00:16:52.030 --> 00:16:53.950
But I won't see him again.

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:57.030
He saw everything.

00:16:57.030 --> 00:16:58.620
- I feel depressed.
- White dolphin!

00:17:01.160 --> 00:17:02.660
Here I come.

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:05.460
Akito, have you been
there all this time?

00:17:06.460 --> 00:17:07.830
I don't know
what you're talking about.

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:10.210
Hayama, she's seen through you.

00:17:12.260 --> 00:17:14.970
Here, I bought you a double
cheeseburger.

00:17:16.470 --> 00:17:17.680
I'll eat with you.

00:17:23.100 --> 00:17:24.520
Sana...

00:17:25.640 --> 00:17:27.980
Sana's been affected.

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:31.110
She likes you.

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:35.240
She still likes you.

00:17:35.570 --> 00:17:38.160
It's the same with you, isn't it?

00:17:38.700 --> 00:17:41.830
You like Sana too, don't you?

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:45.620
Didn't I say I have nothing to do
with her?

00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:48.630
I think
we shouldn't see each other.

00:17:48.630 --> 00:17:52.590
Don't come and see me anymore.

00:17:52.590 --> 00:17:56.050
Please, don't torment me anymore.

00:18:00.100 --> 00:18:02.720
Am I making
things difficult for you?

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:22.030
You forgot your slippers.

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:31.960
I keep hurting Fuka.

00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:54.480
Hayama.

00:18:56.440 --> 00:18:57.990
Hayama.

00:18:59.240 --> 00:19:00.820
The opinionated woman.

00:19:00.820 --> 00:19:04.030
Huh, what?
What are you doing?

00:19:04.030 --> 00:19:07.330
Marathon. Once around Tokyo.

00:19:09.290 --> 00:19:10.540
What's wrong?

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:12.330
What do you mean?

00:19:12.330 --> 00:19:15.340
Why are you
looking at me like that?

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:18.800
Hayama.

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:24.930
I don't like it.
It's the way you used to look.

00:19:39.780 --> 00:19:41.860
What's wrong?

00:19:41.860 --> 00:19:43.780
What about you?

00:19:44.450 --> 00:19:47.040
You look like a lost spirit.

00:19:47.740 --> 00:19:50.870
Ghost is more like it.

00:19:50.870 --> 00:19:52.040
Ghost?

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:54.630
Aren't you an American girl,
Ghost Sana-chan?

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:57.000
Why are you
calling me Sana-chan?

00:19:57.000 --> 00:20:00.170
What? It was hard for me to come up with
such a good name!

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:02.180
It's horrible.
Please spare me already.

00:20:02.180 --> 00:20:05.470
Don't you do that too? You keep
giving people nicknames like Peggy.

00:20:05.470 --> 00:20:08.850
That's not the same thing...
Mine belong in a higher class.

00:20:09.350 --> 00:20:11.230
You have an answer to everything.

00:20:11.230 --> 00:20:12.980
You're really
an opinionated woman.

00:20:12.980 --> 00:20:14.770
So I'm opinionated.

00:20:14.770 --> 00:20:19.070
But why are we hugging
while fighting?

00:20:19.070 --> 00:20:20.440
Who knows.

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:22.900
Like idiots.

00:20:22.900 --> 00:20:24.870
Hey, isn't that Sana-chan?

00:20:24.870 --> 00:20:26.620
No way! Where? Where?

00:20:26.620 --> 00:20:29.160
Maybe they just look alike.

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:30.330
Go on.

00:20:30.910 --> 00:20:35.290
Go on, I'm fine,
don't worry about me.

00:20:36.670 --> 00:20:39.130
Alright, bye.

00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:43.720
Hmm, these two...

00:20:41.760 --> 00:20:46.220
These two...

00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:46.430
- Plate, plate!
- What are you doing, Shimura-san?

00:20:47.100 --> 00:20:48.890
Hey, Sagami.

00:20:48.890 --> 00:20:50.180
Oh, hello.

00:20:50.180 --> 00:20:55.150
What a pain for you.
To have such a self-centered star.

00:20:55.150 --> 00:20:57.150
Oh, not at all...

00:20:57.150 --> 00:20:59.070
Any program today?

00:20:59.070 --> 00:21:00.320
Uh, no.

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:01.780
I feel your pain.

00:21:01.780 --> 00:21:04.650
But sometimes you have to
teach her a lesson.

00:21:04.650 --> 00:21:07.620
Yeah,
or you'll be taken for a ride.

00:21:07.620 --> 00:21:09.870
Um... I have to go. See you later.

00:21:10.950 --> 00:21:14.250
It's not like that.
Not at all like they think.

00:21:15.460 --> 00:21:18.670
Dammit, why does everybody blame
Sana-chan? Uh... What?

00:21:18.670 --> 00:21:19.960
Yikes. How scary.

00:21:19.960 --> 00:21:20.840
Riho-san!

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:23.590
I'm sorry, I was just too angry.

00:21:23.590 --> 00:21:25.180
Nobody understands.

00:21:25.180 --> 00:21:26.680
But I guess it can't be helped.

00:21:26.680 --> 00:21:28.970
Here, you can tell me your
troubles.

00:21:29.220 --> 00:21:30.510
He's hooked!

00:21:30.510 --> 00:21:32.810
No way! I can't believe it.

00:21:32.810 --> 00:21:35.520
Sh... not so loud...

00:21:35.520 --> 00:21:37.230
Anyway that's how it is.

00:21:37.230 --> 00:21:40.360
Sana-chan's not being
self-centered at all.

00:21:40.980 --> 00:21:42.780
For Sana-chan's reputation.

00:21:42.780 --> 00:21:45.570
Bye then. Don't tell anyone!

00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:46.910
I understand!

00:21:46.910 --> 00:21:48.620
Ah! I feel much better.

00:21:52.700 --> 00:21:54.620
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:21:55.210 --> 00:21:57.500
Huh? What's up?

00:21:57.500 --> 00:21:59.670
Naozumi...

00:22:00.750 --> 00:22:02.710
About Sana-chan...

00:22:03.550 --> 00:22:08.970
Sana-chan couldn't say demon...

00:22:08.970 --> 00:22:13.180
...I hear it's because of a boy
called Hayama-kun.

